   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Detailing clear SDG Roadmap</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">SDG Roadmap detailing clear, time-bound targets and action plans, developed through consultations and agency/sectoral plans. The interconnectedness of the SDGs and the interlinkages across the targets means that many of the goals are indivisible. The interactions between the targets can be either synergistic or conflictive, whereby achievement in one goal or target can be detrimental to the achievement of another.  The main Roadmap document will be utilised as a mechanism for integrated solutions to address multidimensional and cross cutting issues to facilitate greater involvement of stakeholders at all levels of decision making towards implementing the SDGs, promoting strategies and policy areas that are at the frontier of development and identify the gaps in development delivery.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2020"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="1"></target>
     <actual value="1"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Implementation guidelines</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Using the SDG framework, two guidelines will be developed; one on localisation and another on SDG-aligned costing and budgeting. Both guidelines are developed to complement and support effective an implementation of the Roadmap. The guidelines will provide recommendations for encouraging more disaggregated data collection and analysis coupled with an inclusive and participatory approach to the implementation of the Roadmap agenda.  Input into the guidelines will be drawn from technical consultations, best practices and guidance with benchmarks and case studies towards building an integrated model for policymakers to align and integrate national development priorities with development planning and solutions, connecting state/local institutional framework with economic development, environmental protection and social development.</narrative>
    </description>
